# ── Data & outputs (code-only repository) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Everything here is either too large for GitHub or fully regenerable by
# re-running the notebooks against Google Earth Engine.

# Rasters -- CLMS IMD ~229 MB each, predicted maps 157-203 MB, GHSL 42-51 MB.
# All exceed GitHub's 100 MB hard limit.
*.tif
*.tiff
*.tif.aux.xml
*.ovr

# Trained models (RF ~21 MB) -- regenerable, and joblib is version-fragile
*.joblib
*.pkl
*.h5

# Sample points, metrics tables, figures
*.gpkg
*.gpkg-shm
*.gpkg-wal
*.shp
*.shx
*.dbf
*.prj
*.cpg
*.qmd
*.csv
*.png
*.jpg
*.pdf

# ...except the handed-over deliverables. The rules above are aimed at the
# figures and tables the notebooks generate; deliverables/ holds the two
# finished documents and is tracked in full. Without this negation the blanket
# *.pdf above silently swallows report.pdf and only the deck gets committed.
!deliverables/
!deliverables/**

# ── Run outputs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every notebook writes under output/, laid out city / dataset / predictor:
#
#   output/milan/{clms,ghsl}/{embedding,median,stack,percentile}/
#   output/{hanoi,hcmc}/{embedding,median}/   per-city rasters and samples
#   output/transfer/{embedding,median}/       the two-city comparison files
#   output/milan/validation/                  photo-interpreted validation
#
# All of it is regenerable by re-running the notebooks against Earth Engine,
# and the predicted rasters exceed GitHub's 100 MB limit on their own.
output/

# ── Input data ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# data/ holds only original inputs now: the CLMS and GHSL reference rasters,
# the Vietnam IMD rasters, the sample points and the photo-interpreted CSVs.
# None of it is ours to redistribute and none of it fits in the repository.
data/

# ── report/ : ignored in full ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing under report/ is tracked. The finished PDF and deck are committed in
# deliverables/ instead, so the repository carries what gets handed over and
# nothing that builds it.
#
# Everything under report/ stays on disk and keeps working -- it is ignored,
# not deleted:
#
#   report.tex     the LaTeX source of the PDF
#   report.pdf     the built report, copied to deliverables/ when finished
#   IMD_Mapping.pptx  the deck, likewise
#
#   facts/         FACTS.md, EXPERIMENT_MAP.md, FIGURES.md, FIGURE_GAPS.md,
#                  OUTLINE.md -- the written record
#   code/          the scripts that build the fact base, the figures and the
#                  decks, and the auditor
#   figs/          every cited figure
#   presentation/  deck sources
#   build/         LaTeX auxiliaries
#   refs.bib       the bibliography
#
# WHAT THIS COSTS, stated plainly so nobody rediscovers it the hard way.
# FACTS.md and the figures are regenerable -- collect_metrics.py and
# make_report_figs.py rebuild them from output/. These are NOT:
#
#   report.tex         the LaTeX source -- the ONLY copy of the report's text
#   EXPERIMENT_MAP.md  hand-written provenance and design decisions
#   OUTLINE.md         hand-written section plan and figure assignments
#   report/code/*.py   the only way to rebuild FACTS.md and the figures
#   refs.bib           hand-maintained bibliography
#
# None of those can be recovered from anything else in the repository. They
# exist on this disk alone, and a fresh clone will not have them. They ARE in
# git history up to the commit that untracked them -- recover with
# `git show <commit>:report/facts/EXPERIMENT_MAP.md`, or
# `git show 024c874:report/report.tex` for the source -- but nothing after
# that point is recorded. Back them up outside git, or track them again.
#
# report.tex matters most here: deliverables/report.pdf is the built output,
# and nothing in the repository can regenerate it. Lose the working copy and
# the report's text is gone from today forward.
report/

docs/

# ── CLAUDE.md ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Project instructions for Claude Code. Ignored at the user's request: it is
# working notes rather than a deliverable. Same caveat as report/facts/ -- it
# is hand-written, nothing regenerates it, and a fresh clone will not have it.
# Earlier versions are recoverable from git history up to the commit that
# untracked it.
CLAUDE.md

# ── Secrets & credentials ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Earth Engine / Google Cloud service-account keys must never be committed.
*.json
!requirements*.json
.env
.env.*
# ...but .env.example is the committed template. It holds no secret, only the
# key names, and without it a fresh clone has nothing to copy from.
!.env.example
credentials/
*-service-account*
.config/earthengine/

# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── Jupyter ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*-checkpoint.ipynb
profile_default/
ipython_config.py

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
install_log.txt
*.log

# ── OS / editor ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
# PowerPoint lock files, written while a deck is open and meaningless once it
# is closed. Anchored to the repo root would miss them; they sit beside the
# deck.
~$*

# Everything under report/ -- the deck sources, the LaTeX auxiliaries, the
# .bbl and .blg BibTeX writes beside report.tex -- is already covered by the
# `report/` rule above, which keeps only the three deliverables.
